docs/feature-inventory.md:12:| Expressions | parentheses; + - * / % and unary +/-, strict-delete; < <= > >=, == != === !==, !; short-circuit &&/\|\|; assignment; conditional `test ? consequent : alternate` | Numeric operators use number-hint ordinary conversion; addition converts both operands with default hint before string/numeric selection. Relational operators convert in source order with number hint, compare two strings by UTF-16 code units, otherwise compare numbers with all NaN comparisons false. Own/inherited valueOf/toString methods work on ordinary objects, arrays and functions; default ordinary objects convert through inherited Object valueOf/toString to [object Object] (numeric NaN). Boolean/String wrappers use their standard payload methods. Number wrappers return numeric payloads for default/number hints and inherited tag strings for string hints. Arrays convert through join; functions convert to exact retained source or the native form. Both operand evaluations precede coercion. === !==, truthiness and Number predicates never coerce. Conditional precedence, selected-arm evaluation and existing bounds remain unchanged. Abstract equality selectively converts at most one object with the default hint; nullish/object and object/object comparisons never coerce. No BigInt, comma, bitwise, update, compound assignment, nullish coalescing or optional chaining. |
docs/feature-inventory.md:16:| Objects | Colon-valued literal entries with word/string keys; dot and computed key get/write; aliases; ordinary methods as function-valued properties; missing properties undefined | Ordinary inherited data properties supported when seeded by the host; production objects inherit their Realm Object root. No accessors, method shorthand, numeric/computed literal keys, spread or enumeration APIs. Guest delete uses unconditional strict-delete: identifier operands are parse errors and nonconfigurable properties throw. Literal __proto__ rejected. Symbol keys retain identity; other primitive keys convert to strings. Object keys use the symbol protocol then string-hint ordinary conversion; default objects key as [object Object]. Primitive property reads/writes reject; delete alone boxes primitives before deferred key conversion. |
docs/feature-inventory.md:21:| Own keys/deletion (TS-004C) | Internal configurable-own deletion, normal false on nonconfigurable rejection, detached lists of all own string keys including nonenumerable keys; canonical array indices first numerically, other strings by creation order. Overwrite preserves position; delete/reinsert renews it. | Key listing remains host-only; TS-025A adds guest strict-delete over current string/symbol keys and Array/String dispatch. No Object/Reflect APIs or generic exotics. Ordinary key listing cannot throw; arrays reuse these operations. |
docs/feature-inventory.md:237:TS-025A adds unconditional strict-delete within this limited profile, not full
